# PCA of the twelve forms of capital, hundred-year slices (data/capital.csv)

MAIN specification: 37 original slices BCE 4100-500 (back-filled 4300/4200 rows excluded),
12 indicators re-standardised within the 37-row frame, ZSichel 0-values kept as observations,
PC1 sign anchored on the only category with perfect sign consistency (symbolic).

## 1. Variance explained and PC1 loadings (MAIN)
PC1 32.4% | PC2 16.4% | PC3 13.7% | PC1+PC2 48.9%

| indicator | category | PC1 loading |
|---|---|---|
| ZKeform (pottery form) | cultural | -0.409 |
| Zkeverz (pottery decoration) | cultural | +0.389 |
| ZCU_AU (copper & gold) | social | +0.367 |
| ZHort (depots) | economic | +0.334 |
| ZBeil (axes & celts) | economic | -0.311 |
| Zamber (amber) | social | -0.287 |
