| Zhausgr (house size) | symbolic | +0.170 |
| ZMonument (monument count) | social | +0.148 |
| ZSichel (sickle) | economic | -0.132 |

Category means of PC1 loadings / sign consistency:
symbolic +0.226 (3/3 positive, consistency 1.00) | social +0.076 (2/3, 0.67) |
cultural -0.010 (1/1, 0.50; mean |loading| 0.399 = largest but split) | economic +0.033 (2/2, 0.50).
Mean within-category r = -0.012 (13 pairs) vs between-category r = +0.057 (53 pairs).
corr(PC1, mean of all 12 standardised indicators) = +0.477; corr(PC1, symbolic composite) = +0.615;
corr(PC1, calendar year) = +0.849 (PC1 is strongly chronological).
=> PC1 is neither a clean "total capital" axis nor a clean single trade-off; it opposes
metals/monuments/depots/houses (positive) against pottery-form diversity, stone axes-celts and amber (negative).
PC2: symbolic 3/3 (+0.236) and social 3/3 (+0.353) positive, cultural and economic split (consistency 0.5)
=> PC2 = symbolic+social display vs pottery decoration/sickle. PC3: symbolic 3/3 negative, economic 3/4.

