## 5. Controls and robustness (out/variant_summary.csv, out/robustness_aligned.csv)
| specification | PC1 EVR | MN | YN | MN-YN |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| MAIN 37 slices, re-standardised, Sichel kept | 0.324 | -1.657 | -1.366 | -0.291 |
| 39 slices incl. back-filled 4300/4200 | 0.303 | -1.374 | -1.117 | -0.257 |
| 37 slices, NOT re-standardised | 0.346 | -1.764 | -1.268 | -0.495 |
| 37 slices, re-standardised, ZSichel dropped | 0.350 | -1.697 | -1.429 | -0.268 |
| 37 slices, NOT re-standardised, ZSichel dropped | 0.355 | -1.773 | -1.283 | -0.490 |
39-row control: PC1 loadings agree in sign 12/12 with MAIN, Spearman rank corr of |loadings| 0.881;
EVR1 falls 0.324 -> 0.303. Back-filled rows do not distort the result.
Leave-one-slice-out (n=37, orientation locked to MAIN): MN-YN -0.470 .. -0.018, MN<YN 37/37,
both phases negative 37/37, EVR1 0.309-0.356.
Leave-one-indicator-out (n=12): MN-YN -0.619 .. +0.272, MN<YN 10/12 (flips when Zamber or ZKeform is dropped),
both phases negative 12/12.
ZMW outlier: capital.csv ZMW = -3.1345 occurs at BCE 4300, 4200 AND 4100 (all group EN); in the 37-row
frame the only occurrence is BCE 4100. Dropping BCE 4100 leaves all 12 loading signs unchanged
(ZMW 0.240 -> 0.332), raises EVR1 to 0.357, but collapses the MN-YN difference to -0.018.
Separate PCA on the 12 MN+YN slices only (n=12, p=12): EVR1 0.434 but loadings agree in sign with MAIN
only 6/12 -> loadings must be estimated on the full series, phases projected.

## 6. Pollen contrast (not part of the PCA)
Chosen column: SMOOTH_MEAN_100y (Belau+Woserin mean, 100-yr smoothing) of
data/pollen_openness_score_Belau_Woserin_Feeser_et_al_2019.csv - published two-site reconstruction,
less exposed to single-core gaps than Belau alone, 100-yr window matches the slice resolution.
  MN -0.479 vs YN -0.569 (EN -2.047, OBA +1.136)
Contrast column pollen_inter_100 (time_series_data.csv, Belau only): MN +0.952 vs YN -0.432
(EN -2.023, OBA +1.209). Same direction (MN higher), much larger amplitude.
Note: with SMOOTH_MEAN_100y both study phases are negative; with pollen_inter_100 MN is positive.
